# Docs Authoring

## Frontmatter

Every doc in `docs/` should start with:

```yaml
---
title: Document Title
status: draft
owner: community
update: January 1, 2026
---
```

- Update `status` to `stable` when reviewed and agreed.
- Set `update` to the last meaningful edit date (`Month D, YYYY`, e.g. `January 1, 2026`).

## Markdown vs MDX

- Use `.md` for normal guidelines.
- Use `.mdx` when the page needs Astro components (e.g. color swatches).
- In MDX, embed swatches with `<ColorCore />` and/or `<ColorSemantic />` (mapped in the docs site — no import required).

## Structure

- One H1 per file (the title).
- Use H2 for major sections, H3 for subsections.
- Keep paragraphs short; use tables and lists for scanability.

## Language

- Plain language; explain terms for beginners.
- **Do** / **Don't** examples where principles apply.
- Active voice; specific instructions over vague advice.

## Linking

- Cross-link related docs in a "Related docs" section at the bottom.
- Use relative paths that match site routes (no `.md` / `.mdx` suffix), e.g. `../vision/design-principles`. Link text for those pages should also omit the extension.
- Files that are **not** Astro pages (token JSON, templates, root `AGENTS.md`, `site/` source) must use GitHub URLs so they do not 404 on the docs site. Keep the filename (including extension) in the link text. Base for docs files: `https://github.com/jcmartinezma/bravo-agentic-design-system/tree/main/docs`.
- When adding or renaming files, update `docs/README.md`.

## Values in examples

- Reference token names, not raw hex or pixel values (unless defining a token).
- Follow `docs/vision/writing-guidelines.md` for UI copy examples.
